            <ArticleTitle>Spondylolisthesis in children and adolescents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-7; quiz 28-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spondylolisthesis in children and adolescents can present in various ways and have a wide range of treatment options. Children are not &quot;little adults.&quot; They require special interview, evaluation, and treatment considerations. This article addresses the characteristics of spondylolisthesis in children and reviews some of the treatment options and related nursing considerations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
